Kills mutant https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4675:

```diff
diff --git a/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp b/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
index 473538e..d484547 100644
--- a/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
+++ b/src/consensus/tx_check.cpp
@@ -32,11 +32,11 @@ bool CheckTransaction(const CTransaction& tx, TxValidationState& state)
     CAmount nValueOut = 0;
     for (const auto& txout : tx.vout)
     {
-        if (txout.nValue < 0)
+        nValueOut += txout.nValue;
+        if (nValueOut < 0)
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-vout-negative");
         if (txout.nValue > MAX_MONEY)
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-vout-toolarge");
-        nValueOut += txout.nValue;
         if (!MoneyRange(nValueOut))
             return state.Invalid(TxValidationResult::TX_CONSENSUS, "bad-txns-txouttotal-toolarge");
     }
```

This mutant could lead to an inflation bug, and the only other check that prevents that is in `GetValueOut`.

This PR kills 3 mutants from https://mutanthub.space/mutants in validation.cpp 
I batched them together because the assertions are within the same test

Mutants killed:

Mutant 4388: validation.cpp ActivateBestChains, && → ||

```diff
@@ -6482,7 +6482,7 @@ util::Result<void> ChainstateManager::ActivateBestChains()
         for (const auto& chainstate : m_chainstates) {
-            if (chainstate && chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
+            if (chainstate || chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
                 chainstates.push_back(chainstate.get());
```

Mutant 4385: validation.cpp GetPruneRange, + 1 → - 1

```diff
@@ -6447,7 +6447,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
-        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight + 1;
+        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight - 1;
```

Mutant 4386: validation.cpp GetPruneRange, - → + MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP

```diff
@@ -6451,7 +6451,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
     int max_prune = std::max<int>(
-        0, m_chain.Height() - static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
+        0, m_chain.Height() + static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
```

The BIP30 tests in `feature_block.py` only cover duplicate coinbase transactions, but the check applies to every transaction in a block.

Add coverage for a duplicate non-coinbase transaction:
- tx A spends coinbase C
- a duplicate of C is mined and matures, so A can be included again
- re-including A is rejected while A's outputs are unspent
- re-including A is accepted after A's outputs are spent

